{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Exile On Main Street and Sticky Fingers fit the bluesy, electric guitar sound I have been enjoying through Clapton and Hendrix; Exile is the album I would choose today.",
    "The Who and Bob Seger also make sense because guitar-driven, rootsy rock appeals to me, while the country recommendation has some connection to my Blown Away listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Donovan, Simon and Garfunkel, and the Lovin' Spoonful lean toward folk, acoustic harmonies, or lighter pop when I currently want electric, blues-influenced music.",
    "The Beatles live album and the hits collections include artists I might enjoy, but those formats are less appealing to me than choosing a studio album for this visit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat familiar older artists as interchangeable, although their sound matters more to me than the era they come from.",
    "Recognizing an artist I might like seems to count too heavily; that alone does not make a live album or greatest-hits collection something I want today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My Clapton and Hendrix listening points toward blues-influenced guitar music, which explains why Exile feels closer to my current mood than gentler folk or pop.",
    "I interact rarely and would choose only one album today, so finding several plausible matches does not mean I would select them all."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in established rock artists but only partly captured my current preference for a bluesy, guitar-driven studio album."
}"}
